# onnxruntime-node (a transitive dependency of @huggingface/transformers) ships
# its CPU binaries inside the npm tarball. Its install script additionally tries
# to download Linux x64 CUDA/GPU binaries from GitHub releases, which fails the
# Amplify (CodeBuild) install with "404 Not Found" because those assets are not
# published for the pinned version. This app only uses onnxruntime-web in the
# browser, so the CUDA provider is never needed. The supported switch below makes
# the installer exit early and keeps `npm ci` deterministic on every platform.
onnxruntime-node-install-cuda=skip
